cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it (and the article)
  as below.
type: software
title: 'vowel-space-model: code for "A mathematical model of the vowel space"'
authors:
  - family-names: Berthommier
    given-names: Frédéric
    email: frederic.berthommier@gipsa-lab.grenoble-inp.fr
    affiliation: Univ. Grenoble Alpes, CNRS, Grenoble INP, GIPSA-lab
repository-code: 'https://github.com/FBerthommier/vocalic-spaces'
abstract: >-
  Python translation and reproduction package of the simulations of the
  article "A mathematical model of the vowel space": three-phase mixing
  function, coordination function, generic / DRM / Fant vocal-tract
  models, Badin transmission-line formant computation, LPC vowel
  resynthesis, Monte-Carlo C1/C2 conditions, figures and multimedia.
keywords:
  - speech production
  - vowel space
  - vocal tract modeling
  - transmission line model
  - formants
  - articulatory-acoustic inversion
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-10-02'
